# Links lychee should not check, with the reason. Regexes, one per line.

# GitHub compare views between two release tags.
#
# release-please writes its changelog heading as a compare link for the version
# it is about to create — `compare/v0.1.0...v0.1.1` — and that tag does not
# exist until the release pull request merges. Checking it *on* that pull
# request asks whether a tag exists before the thing that creates it has run,
# so it 404s on every release, forever. The first release escaped it only
# because an initial version has no previous tag to compare against.
#
# The cost of this line is that a compare link written by hand, in prose, is no
# longer checked. That is a small and stated loss; the alternative is a link
# checker that is red on every release PR and therefore ignored.
https://github\.com/.+/compare/
